mework provides the classes needed for your apps to communicate with Blueto=
oth-equipped low energy (LE) and Basic Rate / Enhanced Data Rate (BR/EDR) w=
ireless technology.</p><p>Don=E2=80=99t subclass any of the classes of the =
Core Bluetooth framework. Overriding these classes isn=E2=80=99t supported =
and results in undefined behavior.</p><p>Core Bluetooth background executio=
n modes aren=E2=80=99t supported in iPad apps running on macOS.</p><p>In iO=
S 26 and later, your app can continue certain activities in the background =
if the app starts a Live Activity before it goes to the background. If your=
 app has an instantiated <a href=3D"https://developer.apple.com/documentati=
on/corebluetooth/cbmanager" class=3D"inline-link"><code data-v-880086a2=3D"=
">CBManager</code></a> and starts a Live Activity, it can use the same priv=
ileges while in the background that it uses when it is in the foreground. T=
his means activities like scanning without providing service UUID=E2=80=99s=
 and scanning with duplicates filter disabled will be allowed while in the =
background. For more information about creating Live Activities, see <a hre=
f=3D"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ActivityKit" class=3D"inline=
-link">ActivityKit</a>.</p><aside data-v-5ed0444c=3D"" aria-label=3D"import=
ant" class=3D"important"><p data-v-5ed0444c=3D"" class=3D"label">Important<=
/p><p data-v-5ed0444c=3D""> Your app will crash if its <code data-v-880086a=
2=3D"" class=3D"inline-code" data-v-5ed0444c=3D"">Info<wbr data-v-880086a2=
=3D"">.plist</code> doesn=E2=80=99t include usage description keys for the =
types of data it needs to access. To access Core Bluetooth APIs on apps lin=
ked on or after iOS 13, include the <a href=3D"https://developer.apple.com/=
documentation/bundleresources/information-property-list/nsbluetoothalwaysus=
agedescription" class=3D"inline-link" data-v-5ed0444c=3D""><code data-v-880=
086a2=3D"">NSBluetooth<wbr data-v-880086a2=3D"">Always<wbr data-v-880086a2=
=3D"">Usage<wbr data-v-880086a2=3D"">Description</code></a> key. In iOS 12 =
and earlier, include <a href=3D"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/b=
undleresources/information-property-list/nsbluetoothperipheralusagedescript=
ion" class=3D"inline-link" data-v-5ed0444c=3D""><code data-v-880086a2=3D"">=
NSBluetooth<wbr data-v-880086a2=3D"">Peripheral<wbr data-v-880086a2=3D"">Us=
age<wbr data-v-880086a2=3D"">Description</code></a> to access Bluetooth per=
ipheral data.</p></aside></div></div></div><section data-v-68542180=3D"" da=
